-- title:
--   Formal smoothness of the descended chart B₀ over A∩ k₀
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$, a nonzero level $M'$, a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, a finite set $W$ of places of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A, M')$ over $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$, an inclusion $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M' \le \mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ of the base-changed modular function field of level $M'$ into the base-changed $x_H$-function field of level $(q^2M', \mathrm{levelH}\,q\,M')$, a constant reduction $R_0$ of $A$ on $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ with residue field $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}$, and a place $s \in W$. Fix further an intermediate field $k_0$ of $\mathbb Q \subset \overline{\mathbb Q}$, elements $\pi_0$ (with image in $A$), $\zeta_0$, $\varpi_t$, $\xi$ of $k_0$, a natural number $\ell$, an intermediate field $K_b$ of $k_0 \subset \overline{\mathbb Q}$ with a valuation subring $A_b$ cut out by $A$ and an element $\varpi_b$, a prime $\ell'$, an intermediate field $K_{\ell}$ of $k_0 \subset k_0(\!(t)\!)$ carrying an algebra and scalar-tower structure over $O := A \cap k_0$ (the comap of $A$ along $k_0 \to \overline{\mathbb Q}$), a nonzero $j_\ell \in K_\ell$, an element $\varpi_t' \in O$, an ideal $y$ of the finite chart algebra $\mathrm{chartAlgFin}\,O\,K_\ell\,j_\ell$, an $O$-subalgebra $B_t$ of $K_\ell$ contained in a valuation subring $W_t$ of $K_\ell$, naturals $n, m$, a matrix $\gamma_0 \in \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb Z)$, a $k_0$-automorphism $\tau_0$ of $K_\ell$, an element $\zeta_c$ of the adic completion of $O$ at its maximal ideal, a proof that $\mathrm{jqNModC}\,k_0\,(q\ell') \in K_\ell$, an element $a_0 \in O$, a finite set $\mathrm{ends}$ of subrings of $K_\ell$, and a term $\mathcal F$ of the rigid-descent hypothesis package $\mathrm{RigidDescentHyps}$ for all these data. Let $G$ be the subgroup of $\mathrm{Aut}_{k_0}(K_\ell)$ generated by those $\tau$ for which some $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ satisfies $\mathrm{IsLevelAutAt}\,k_0\,(q\ell')\,\xi\,(q\ell')\,((q\ell')^2M')\,(\mathrm{levelH}\,(q\ell')\,M')\,\gamma^{-1}\,K_\ell\,\tau$, i.e. $\tau$ acts on every quotient of integral $q$-expansions of weight-$k$ forms on $\Gamma_H((q\ell')^2M')$ as the slash by $\mathrm{conjElemN}\,m\,\gamma^{-1}$, under every embedding $k_0 \to \mathbb C$ sending $\xi$ to $e^{2\pi i/(q\ell')}$. Let $K_0$ be the fixed field of $G$, let $B_0$ be the $O$-subalgebra of elements of $B_t$ fixed by all of $G$, and let $W_0'$ be the valuation subring of $K_0$ cut out by $W_t$. The conclusion is that $B_0$ is formally smooth over $O = A \cap k_0$.
--
--   This is the formal-smoothness assertion for the Galois descent of the rigid supersingular affine chart: the invariant subalgebra $B_0 = B_t^G$ of the chart on the auxiliary level $q\ell'$ is formally smooth over the constants $A \cap k_0$. It is one of the defining properties of the descended chart, and is used in assembling the supersingular affine chart over the discrete valuation ring $A \cap k_0$ in [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.supersingularDVR_affineChart_invariants_of_rigidChart_framed`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.supersingularDVR_affineChart_invariants_of_rigidChart_framed).
